\section*{The Graphic Kahn–Kalai Conjecture}

\subsection{OpenAI's claim}
\textit{The second Kahn--Kalai bound}: The claimed graph containment threshold is at most $C p_{\mathrm E}(n,H)(1+\log_2 |E(H)|)$ for every nonempty graph $H$ fitting inside the host vertex set. The constant is universal.

\subsection{Outline of the argument}
\textit{The second Kahn--Kalai bound}: A maximizing-core selection creates nested subgraphs whose added-edge distributions have controlled conditional probabilities. Copies of these cores form a tree of disjoint increment labels with geometrically changing sizes. Bayesian resampling compares planted and posterior labels, and iteration across the tree turns the spread control into the logarithmic containment bound.

\subsection{Scope relative to this problem}
\textit{The second Kahn--Kalai bound}: The sharper edge-count theorem gives p\_c(n,H)<=A p\_E(n,H)(1+log\_2 e(H)). Since e(H)<=binom(v(H),2), this is at most K p\_E log v(H) for one universal K on graphs with an edge. The empty graph has trivial containment probability one. Thus it reaches the question log v(H) factor rather than only log n.

This page records partial support. Complete resolution of the catalogue question is not established by this record.

\subsection{Formal verification}
Family 176 describes Lean coverage for the nonempty graph containment-threshold comparison with the edge-count logarithm.

\textit{The second Kahn--Kalai bound}: The manuscript links \texttt{SecondKahnKalai.lean} (declaration \texttt{OAI.LeanBlast.SecondKahnKalai.secondKahnKalaiBounds}).

The documented selection includes this manuscript’s main assertion; that assertion retains the restrictions stated above.

This site has not run the Lean development. These links describe OpenAI’s selected formal statements and should be read with their stated scope.

\subsection{Status caveat}
OpenAI reports that an internal model produced the manuscripts. Their arguments have not been independently verified as proofs by this site. Any portion outside the documented formal scope may contain mistakes, and the catalogue label reports the announced mathematical claim.

